  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 47. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 御馳走 — 人をもてなすための食事やおいしい料理。\n2. ゴンドラ — ロープウエーなどで人を乗せる箱形の設備。\n3. ゴーカート — 低い車体で走る小さな自動車。\n4. ゴールキーパー — サッカーなどでゴールを守る役の選手。\n5. 再会 — 離れていた人とまた会うこと。\n6. 再起動 — 機械やコンピューターをいったん止めて動かし直すこと。\n7. 最強 — いちばん強いこと。\n8. サイクリング — 自転車に乗って走ることを楽しむこと。\n9. サイクル — 同じ順序で繰り返す一巡り。\n10. 歳月 — 過ぎていく年月。\n11. 最古 — 最も古いこと。\n12. 最高級 — 等級の中で最も上であること。\n13. 最後尾 — 並んだもののいちばん後ろ。\n14. 最小 — 最も小さいこと。\n15. 菜食 — 野菜などの植物性の食べ物を食べること。\n16. サイズ — 大きさや寸法。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
